# Phoenix OS — Disk Tools Package List
# PhotoRec is bundled with testdisk — recovers photos, docs, videos by signature
# RAID management
# S.M.A.R.T. monitoring and disk health
# SAFETY REMINDER: Phoenix OS enforces a safety model for disk operations.
# See docs/security-model.md for full policy details.
# These cover additional filesystem types:
# These tools are the core of Phoenix OS's recovery mission.
# USB and removable media
aureport           # Linux audit system report generator
autopsy            # TODO: Autopsy GUI (large; consider as optional Flatpak)
balena-etcher      # TODO: Add as Flatpak in 070-flatpak.list or via AppImage
binwalk            # Firmware and binary analysis/extraction
bless              # GUI hex editor
blkid              # Block device identification
bonnie++           # Filesystem benchmark
brasero            # Disc burning GUI (GNOME, but usable on KDE)
ca-certificates
cdrdao             # CD/DVD recording
cryptsetup         # (also in disk-tools; LUKS volume management)
cryptsetup         # LUKS full-disk encryption management
curl
dc3dd              # (also in disk-tools; forensic dd with hashing)
dc3dd              # Enhanced dd for forensic imaging (with hashing)
ddrescue           # (also in disk-tools; primary tool for failing drive imaging)
ddrescue           # GNU ddrescue: recovers data from failing drives
dmraid             # Device-mapper RAID (Intel RST, NVIDIA nForce RAID)
dvdbackup          # DVD backup utility
exiftool           # Read/write EXIF data (media file analysis)
ext4magic          # More powerful ext3/ext4 deleted file recovery
extundelete        # Recover deleted files from ext3/ext4 filesystems
fatcat             # FAT filesystem deleted file recovery and analysis
fdisk              # Classic MBR partition tool (also handles GPT)
fio                # Flexible I/O tester: storage benchmarking
firmware-iwlwifi
firmware-linux
firmware-linux-nonfree
firmware-realtek
foremost           # File carving by file header/footer signatures
gdisk              # GPT fdisk: GPT-aware partition tool (gdisk, sgdisk, cgdisk)
genisoimage        # ISO creation
ghex               # GNOME hex editor (usable on KDE)
git
gparted            # GParted: graphical partition editor (gold standard)
hashcat            # Password recovery (for legally-owned encrypted volumes)
hdparm             # ATA disk parameters: speed test, power management
hexyl              # Hex viewer with visual byte classification
htop
iozone3            # File system benchmark
john               # John the Ripper: password auditing
jpeg-archive       # JPEG optimization (useful for recovering partially-written images)
kde-standard
last               # Login history from wtmp
libimage-exiftool-perl  # Perl ExifTool library
libpst-utils       # Outlook PST file extraction (readpst)
logwatch           # (also in repair-tools)
lsblk              # (part of util-linux, should already be present)
lvm2               # Logical Volume Manager
magicrescue        # Recovers files by "magic bytes" recipes
mdadm              # Linux software RAID management
memtest86+         # RAM testing (GRUB-level; also runnable post-boot)
mp3val             # MP3 validation and repair
mpack              # MIME message packing/unpacking
network-manager-gnome
ntfsundelete       # NTFS deleted file recovery (part of ntfs-3g)
nvme-cli           # NVMe management CLI (nvme list, nvme smart-log, etc.)
partclone          # Partition-level cloning (filesystem-aware)
parted             # GNU parted: scriptable partition management
partimage          # Partition imaging tool
pciutils
pgdump             # TODO: Add PostgreSQL recovery tools if demand warrants
plasma-workspace-wayland
safecopy           # Alternative to dd for damaged media
safecopy           # Copy files/devices, skipping bad sectors gracefully
scalpel            # High-performance file carver (faster than foremost for large disks)
sfdisk             # Scriptable partition table tool
sleuthkit          # The Sleuth Kit: filesystem forensic analysis
smartmontools      # smartctl, smartd — ATA and NVMe S.M.A.R.T.
sqlite3            # SQLite database inspection and repair
squashfs-tools     # SquashFS: inspect and create squashfs (ISO/live analysis)
strings            # Extract printable strings from binary files
testdisk           # (also in repair-tools; handles partition + file recovery)
unar               # Universal archive extractor (handles corrupted archives)
usb-creator-gtk    # Ubuntu USB startup disk creator
usbutils
util-linux         # Core disk utilities: lsblk, blkid, losetup, mount, etc.
vim
wayland-protocols
wipefs             # Wipe filesystem signatures (requires confirmation in UI)
xxd                # Hex dump utility
plymouth
plymouth-themes
sddm
